<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Privacy Policy · Socio</title>
  <script src="https://cdn.tailwindcss.com"></script>
</head>
<body class="bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 min-h-screen flex flex-col">
  <header class="border-b border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/70 backdrop-blur">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-3 flex items-center justify-between">
      <a href="/" class="font-bold text-lg tracking-tight">
        <span class="text-violet-400">socio</span><span class="text-slate-500">.dev</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/login" class="text-sm text-slate-400 hover:text-slate-100">Sign in</a>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main class="flex-1 max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10 w-full">
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-2">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 mb-8">Last updated: 2026-08-11</p>

    <div class="space-y-6 text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
      <section>
        <h2 class="font-semibold text-slate-100 mb-1">1. What we store</h2>
        <p>To operate the Service we store: your username and a password hash, platform connection tokens (used to publish on your behalf), and the posts and media you schedule. All data is stored in a local SQLite database on the server that runs the Service.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="font-semibold text-slate-100 mb-1">2. Passwords</h2>
        <p>Passwords are stored as salted, key-stretched hashes (scrypt). They are never stored in plain text and can never be recovered; a new password must be set by the operator if forgotten.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="font-semibold text-slate-100 mb-1">3. Sessions</h2>
        <p>Login uses a signed, HTTP-only cookie. It expires after 30 days. We do not use third-party tracking cookies.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="font-semibold text-slate-100 mb-1">4. Third-party platforms</h2>
        <p>When you connect an account (LinkedIn, Meta, Google, TikTok), the connection is made with that provider's authorization flow and their terms apply. The Service publishes content through their APIs using the tokens you authorize. Each provider's privacy policy governs data they collect during those flows.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="font-semibold text-slate-100 mb-1">5. Media and content</h2>
        <p>Media you upload for scheduling is stored on the server and only exposed through authenticated endpoints. It is never shared with third parties except the platform you explicitly select as a posting target.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="font-semibold text-slate-100 mb-1">6. Deletion</h2>
        <p>Request removal of your account from the operator and your account, tokens, and scheduled content will be deleted from the database.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="font-semibold text-slate-100 mb-1">7. Changes</h2>
        <p>This policy may be updated from time to time. Continued use after changes constitutes acceptance.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>

  <footer class="border-t border-slate-800 py-4 text-center text-xs text-slate-600">
    socio · <a href="/terms" class="underline">Terms of Service</a> · <a href="/privacy" class="underline">Privacy Policy</a>
  </footer>
</body>
</html>
